{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Come now, let me come in to you.</b> The verse should properly have said הבי (feminine), but because she was in his eyes a harlot making the demand with her mouth, after the manner of the male, therefore Scripture altered and spoke to her in the masculine form. We find a similar case (Genesis 19): ״לכה נשקה״ — masculine, when it should have said לכי — and I explained it there."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:36.686625746Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}